  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "n-p1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 900,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "1 \u00b7 LANDING AND SIGN IN\nRead left to right \u2014 this is the whole first-visit path.\nA stranger lands, learns what the branch is, joins with four fields, gets an email link, and is in.\nNo password anywhere in this flow, by design."
    },
    {
      "id": "n-p1b",
      "x": 1580,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 760,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "Four fields only: name, Tech-U email, department (Mechanical or Mechatronics), level (100\u2013500).\nInstitution is never asked \u2014 the tech-u.edu.ng address already answers it."
    },
    {
      "id": "n-p2",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 900,
      "page": "page-2",
      "text": "2 \u00b7 MEMBERSHIP, END TO END\nScreen 5 is what the new member sees while waiting. Screens 6 and 7 are the same moment from the executive's side.\nScreen 8 is the member the evening they are approved; screen 9 is the record itself, months later."
    },
    {
      "id": "n-p2b",
      "x": 1580,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 1600,
      "page": "page-2",
      "text": "The executive's job here is one comparison: does this matric number appear on the department roll?\nThe queue answers it for them \u2014 'On list' or 'Not found' \u2014 so approving is a glance, not an investigation.\nThat only works if the HOD shares the roll. It is an open question in the plan (design plan section 17.7)."
    },
    {
      "id": "n-p3",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 900,
      "page": "page-3",
      "text": "3 \u00b7 QUICK JOIN\nOne link to drop in a WhatsApp group or print as a QR on a flyer.\nSame four fields as the full sign up, no landing page in the way, and it carries who shared it."
    },
    {
      "id": "n-p4",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 900,
      "page": "page-4",
      "text": "MOBILE (v1)\nThe earlier phone screens, kept as they are.\nThey come back once the desktop flows are settled \u2014 the token layer is shared, so they follow."
    }
  ],
